,title,link,text,language,family
0,Benue–Congo languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benue–Congo_languages,"Benue–Congo is a major branch of the Volta-Congo languages which covers most of Sub-Saharan Africa.The neighbouring Volta–Niger branch of Nigeria and Benin is sometimes called ""West Benue–Congo"", but it does not form a united branch with Benue–Congo.",Baangi,Niger-Congo
1,Baangi jezik – Wikipedija,https://hr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baangi_jezik,"Baangi jezik (ISO 639-3: bqx; cibaangi), nigersko-kongoanski jezik uže skupine kainji, kojim govori 15 000 ljudi (1996) na sjeveru nigerijske države Niger.",Baangi,Niger-Congo
2,Baangi Language (BQX) – L1 & L2 Speakers... | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/bqx/,Baangi is an endangered indigenous language of Nigeria. It belongs to the Niger-Congo language family. The language is used as a first language by adults only.,Baangi,Niger-Congo
3,Baangi language,https://grokipedia.com/page/baangi_language,"In Baangi, a Kainji language of the Niger-Congo family spoken in Niger State, Nigeria, adjectives form a closed class that modifies nouns through agreement in noun class and number.",Baangi,Niger-Congo
4,Baangi - bqx (Niger-Congo) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/bqx/,"People Groups who primarily speak Baangi. To download a comprehensive people group list in spreadsheet form, visit our Research Data page. Visualize lostness with powerful maps.",Baangi,Niger-Congo
5,Niger-Congo-Benue-Congo,https://lingweb.eva.mpg.de/channumerals/Niger-Congo-Benue-Congo.htm,"The Niger-Congo Language Phylum Benue-Congo languages. Akpes: Akpes. BantoidKainji Lakeː Laru, Lopa,Tsucuba. Kambariː Baangi, Tsishingini, Tsikimba (Ashen), Tsuvadi.",Baangi,Niger-Congo
6,Niger-Congo languages - Sorosoro Sorosoro,https://www.sorosoro.org/en/niger-congo-languages/,"The Niger-Congo family counts between 1 300 and 1 500 languages, depending on the classifications, representing alone nearly a quarter of the planet’s languages.",Baangi,Niger-Congo
7,"Full text of ""pmswiki-Lenga_Baangi-20200725.pdf""",https://archive.org/stream/pmswiki-Lenga_Baangi-20200725.pdf/pmswiki-Lenga_Baangi-20200725_djvu.txt,La lenga Baangi o Baangi a fa part die lenghe niger-kordofanian-e e a I'e parla specialment an Nigeria . IT. Aiuto per la lettura. lenghe Atlantic-Congo lenghe Volta-Congo lenghe Benue-Congo lenghe Kainji. lenghe Ossidentaj lenga Baangi. Cod...,Baangi,Niger-Congo
8,Baangi in Nigeria people group profile | Joshua Project,https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/10533/NI,"The Baangi people live in northern Niger State, in Nigeria. They are centered around Bangi town which is south of Bena. The Baangi use Hausa predominantly for daily activities in their community.",Baangi,Niger-Congo
9,Niger-Congo Language Family - Structure & Writing - MustGo,https://www.mustgo.com/worldlanguages/niger-congo-language-family/,"The earliest evidence of a Niger-Congo language dates back to Portuguese records of the 16th century. However, few grammars were published prior to the 19th century although the first known grammar of an African language (Kongo) was written by an Italian missionary in 1659.",Baangi,Niger-Congo
